gions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollback status: rolled_out. v2.3.0 was selected as the most recent release with a healthy production status (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging). Follow-up needed: confirm health/error rate recovery on v2.3.0 and investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before re-deploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n1. **Assessed the service**: checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Identified the rollback target**: v2.3.0 \u2014 the most recent release marked healthy in *production*. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy but only in staging, so I excluded it.)\n3. **Rolled back** checkout-api to v2.3.0 in all three production regions \u2014 status: `rolled_out`.\n4. **Opened incident INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) describing the failure and the rollback; the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\nRecommended follow-up: verify the error rate recovers on v2.3.0 and root-cause the v2.3.1 failure before attempting a redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}